1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
One sky. The Chinese saw — a cowherd and
a weaver, split by a river.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:10,000
The two small stars beside him? Legend
says they’re his carrying pole, with
their two children.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Northern Hemisphere, August evenings —
the brightest star nearly overhead.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Between them, in dark skies, a misty
band: the Milky Way.

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:25,000
Add Deneb, and the three make the Summer
Triangle.

6
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:31,000
Meet once a year? Even light takes 14.6
years, one way.

7
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Often said to be Deneb, in Tianjin — the
“Heavenly Ford” of the sky’s river.

8
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Happy Qixi! One sky. Different peoples,
different stories.

9
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:45,000
Follow for a new sky every week.

